      "location": "lib/features/auth/presentation/cubit/auth_state.dart:101-104 (toString, c35f704)",
      "trigger_condition": "`AuthState.toString()` interpolates the raw `password` field: `'AuthState(mode: $mode, email: $email, password: $password, ...)'`. `AuthCubit.passwordChanged` emits a fresh `AuthState` on every keystroke.",
      "guard_snippet": "Redact `password` in `toString()`, e.g. `password: ${password.isEmpty ? '' : '•'.padLeft(password.length, '•')}`, the same way most Bloc states mask secrets.",
      "potential_consequence": "Nothing in this epic prints a state transition today, but the moment any later `BlocObserver`/log line/crash reporter — a near-universal Flutter debugging pattern — calls `transition.toString()`, the user's plaintext password starts leaking into logs one keystroke at a time."
    },
    {
      "location": "lib/core/navigation/expiry_overlay_host.dart:99-104 combined with lib/features/auth/data/repositories/session_repository_impl.dart:111-114 (_onSessionExpired, c35f704)",
      "trigger_condition": "If `widget.navigatorKey.currentState?.overlay?.context` is null at the exact post-frame callback when `expired` fires, `_onStatus` resets `_expiryOverlayShown = false` and gives up silently. But `_onSessionExpired()` only emits `SessionStatus.expired` on the transition *from* `authenticated` — once `_lastStatus` is already `expired`, no later AUTH_EXPIRED signal from any other in-flight request can re-trigger `statusStream` to retry showing the overlay.",
      "guard_snippet": "On a null overlay context, retry on the next frame (or next `WidgetsBinding` post-frame callback loop) instead of giving up for the whole `expired` episode, since nothing else will ever re-arm this path.",
      "potential_consequence": "If the overlay's one attempt happens to race a Navigator rebuild, the user is left on the authenticated screen with an actually-dead session and zero visual indication — no overlay, no error, nothing — until they manually restart the app."
    },
    {
      "location": "lib/core/di/injection_container.dart:27-28 (c35f704) combined with main.dart's try/catch around setupCoreDependencies()",
      "trigger_condition": "`dotenv.get('FUNCTIONS_BASE_URL')`/`dotenv.get('SUPABASE_ANON_KEY')` only throw when the *key* is missing from `.env` — a `.env` with the keys present but blank (exactly the shape `.env.example` ships, `FUNCTIONS_BASE_URL=`) passes silently.",
      "guard_snippet": "After `dotenv.get(...)`, assert/throw on an empty string too (`if (functionsBaseUrl.isEmpty) throw ...`) so the existing, purpose-built `main.dart` catch block (which already prints a friendly 'copy .env.example and fill in real values' message) actually catches this case.",
      "potential_consequence": "The app boots fully, registers every dependency successfully, and only fails much later and far less legibly — inside `UrlBuilder.build`/dio, building a URL fragment like `/auth-login` with no host — instead of at the one place already designed to explain the real problem clearly."
    },
    {
      "location": "lib/core/widgets/confirmation_dialog.dart:57 (static `isOpen` guard, c35f704) — shared across every future caller by design (see this file's own class doc: \"a later story (Epic 8's account-deletion confirm) reuses this same widget\")",
      "trigger_condition": "`isOpen` is a single process-wide static flag gating every `ConfirmationDialog.show()` call from any feature. It's released only via `whenComplete`/the catch-block's `rethrow` path — both of which assume the dialog's route eventually completes or the call itself throws synchronously.",
      "guard_snippet": "Scope the single-overlay guard per call site (or add a hard timeout / explicit reset hook) rather than one global static boolean shared by unrelated features across epics.",
      "potential_consequence": "If any call site's dialog route is ever torn down without completing normally (e.g. a future navigation change that replaces the Navigator mid-dialog), `isOpen` sticks `true` forever and silently blocks every *other* feature's confirmation dialog app-wide — e.g. Story 1.5's session-expiry overlay getting stuck open would later block Story 8.5's account-deletion confirmation from ever showing, with no connection between the two obvious from either call site."
    },
    {
      "location": "lib/core/network/header_interceptor.dart:53-67 (onRequest's catch around readAccessToken) combined with lib/core/network/api_client.dart's _mapDioException (c35f704)",
      "trigger_condition": "A thrown platform exception from the secure-storage channel while reading the access token is caught and treated identically to 'no token stored' — the request proceeds with no `Authorization` header at all on a `bearerAuth` call. The backend then returns an auth-failure code (no valid token), which `ApiClient._mapDioException` maps to `AuthExpired` and — since this isn't one of the three anon-key-only functions — unconditionally calls `_sessionExpiryNotifier.notifyExpired()`.",
      "guard_snippet": "Distinguish 'the platform channel glitched reading the token' from 'there truly is no token' — e.g. surface the former as a `malformedResponse`/local failure that the caller can retry, rather than letting it silently degrade into a request that will be read by the backend (and by `ApiClient`) as a genuine session expiry.",
      "potential_consequence": "A transient secure-storage read glitch (plausible on iOS, e.g. the keychain briefly unavailable right after the app resumes from background) gets indistinguishable from an actual dead session: the user sees the full 'Sessão expirada' recovery overlay and is pushed toward re-authenticating even though their session was never actually invalid."
    },
    {
      "location": "lib/features/auth/data/repositories/session_repository_impl.dart:130-139 (restoreSession's 'no stored refresh token' branch, c35f704)",
      "trigger_condition": "A fresh install / post-logout boot (no refresh token ever stored) returns `left(const Failure.authExpired(message: 'No stored session to restore'))` — the exact same `Failure` subtype a backend-confirmed dead token produces a few lines below, even though the two events ('never had a session' vs. 'had one, server says it's dead') are semantically distinct.",
      "guard_snippet": "Either introduce a distinct no-op/none-stored outcome (even if it's just a different message or a dedicated local marker the caller can branch on) or make it explicit in the `SessionRepository` contract that `restoreSession()`'s `Left` is not meant to be pattern-matched by `Failure` subtype, only read as a boolean outcome.",
      "potential_consequence": "Nothing in this epic currently reads this particular `Left` (main.dart discards it), but the very first future consumer that pattern-matches on `Failure` subtype to decide UI (e.g. showing an auth-expired toast) will fire that same messaging on every single fresh install, not just on an actual expired session."
    }
  ]
